    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8418" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεπι-σήμαντος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>undistinguished,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ τὴν ἐσθῆτα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					5.81.3
				</span></i>
			; <i>unrecorded, unnoticed,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τινα</span> or 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τι παραλιπεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					11.2.1
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				11.59
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Sign.</u>
				34
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>
			<i>without notice,</i> Aps.<i><span class="en">
				p.259H.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>without an attack of</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπισημασία</span> (q.v.), <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.277
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>not conferring distinction,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοφοῖς ἀνδράσι</span> Dariusap.<i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				9.14
			</span></i>.</div>
